[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186188275 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188535 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two independent continuous random variables whose marginal density functions are as follows:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3y, & \\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\le 0.5,Y\\le \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}).$" :question/worked-solution "Two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability density functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nSince our random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot 3y \\\\  & =6xy,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $(x,y)\\in [0,1]\\times [1,\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}].$ Therefore, the full expression for $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6xy, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 0.5,Y\\le 1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.5}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2/3}}6xy\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.5}6x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2/3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.5}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{0.5} \\\\  & =(0.5)^{2}-0 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185490 :answer-field/correct 17592186185493 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188561 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two independent continuous random variables whose marginal density functions are as follows:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}y, & \\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(0\\le X\\le 0.4,Y\\le 2).$ Round your answer to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability density functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nSince our random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}y \\\\  & =y\\sqrt{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $(x,y)\\in [0,1]\\times [1,2].$ Therefore, the full expression for $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\sqrt{x}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X\\le 0.4,Y\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.4}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.4}\\sqrt{x}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.4}\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{0.4} \\\\  & =(0.4)^{3/2}-0 \\\\  & ≈0.253.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185646 :answer-field/correct 17592186185650 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86" :question/id #uuid "1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86" :question/math-academy-id "q-143364" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two independent continuous random variables whose marginal density functions are as follows:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & \\,0\\le x, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}y, & \\,3\\le y\\le 5, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\ge 2,3\\le Y\\le 4).$" :question/worked-solution "Two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability density functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nSince our random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}y{e}^{-x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $(x,y)\\in [0,\\infty )\\times [3,5].$ Therefore, the full expression for $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}y{e}^{-x}, & \\,0\\le x,\\,3\\le y\\le 5 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2,3\\le Y\\le 4) & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }[{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{8}y{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{8}{e}^{-x}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{3}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{16}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{b}\\frac{7}{16}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{7{e}^{-x}}{16}]}_{2}^{b} \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to \\infty }[-\\frac{7{e}^{-b}}{16}+\\frac{7{e}^{-2}}{16}] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{16{e}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8f6c7f06-285b-5716-8654-ada585b5cad3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ca1210b-5ee2-5865-924d-eb975f41a198" "answer-e274eb34-e730-5088-9d44-3c0f08b82dba" "answer-8f6c7f06-285b-5716-8654-ada585b5cad3" "answer-22b3a3fc-340b-5ed5-8d5e-990986db2466" "answer-411a9cec-3a8e-59f5-9ad3-e086842f889a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ca1210b-5ee2-5865-924d-eb975f41a198" :answer/id #uuid "6ca1210b-5ee2-5865-924d-eb975f41a198" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e274eb34-e730-5088-9d44-3c0f08b82dba" :answer/id #uuid "e274eb34-e730-5088-9d44-3c0f08b82dba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16{e}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f6c7f06-285b-5716-8654-ada585b5cad3" :answer/id #uuid "8f6c7f06-285b-5716-8654-ada585b5cad3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16{e}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22b3a3fc-340b-5ed5-8d5e-990986db2466" :answer/id #uuid "22b3a3fc-340b-5ed5-8d5e-990986db2466" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-411a9cec-3a8e-59f5-9ad3-e086842f889a" :answer/id #uuid "411a9cec-3a8e-59f5-9ad3-e086842f889a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8{e}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188295 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb" "question-09b415e6-d89a-5c4c-91d7-faeef6a95b62"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb" :question/id #uuid "02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-143377" :question/problem "The joint probability density function for the continuous random variables  $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{2}{3}y$ for $y\\in [1,2]$\n\nII. $f(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent" :question/worked-solution "Two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability density functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the marginal density function for $Y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}y{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $y\\in [1,2].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the marginal density function for $X,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}(2-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $x\\in [0,1].$ So, when $x\\in [0,1]$ and $y\\in [1,2],$ we obtain that \n\n$$\n{{\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y}_{⏟}}_{f(x,y)}={{(4{x}^{3})}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{X}(x)}\\cdot {{(\\frac{2}{3}y)}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-94c5f700-7024-5ad9-9fb8-06de616c6958" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fbb5fdb8-bd3a-507b-bfd0-0f58c8d15589" "answer-8a10c141-494b-5ffe-b789-4d235572d460" "answer-94c5f700-7024-5ad9-9fb8-06de616c6958" "answer-a350e58a-9fe9-5a48-a78c-f6ab313c004a" "answer-f085a1c6-cfcd-5341-bcfa-3848ba092d59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbb5fdb8-bd3a-507b-bfd0-0f58c8d15589" :answer/id #uuid "fbb5fdb8-bd3a-507b-bfd0-0f58c8d15589" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a10c141-494b-5ffe-b789-4d235572d460" :answer/id #uuid "8a10c141-494b-5ffe-b789-4d235572d460" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94c5f700-7024-5ad9-9fb8-06de616c6958" :answer/id #uuid "94c5f700-7024-5ad9-9fb8-06de616c6958" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a350e58a-9fe9-5a48-a78c-f6ab313c004a" :answer/id #uuid "a350e58a-9fe9-5a48-a78c-f6ab313c004a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f085a1c6-cfcd-5341-bcfa-3848ba092d59" :answer/id #uuid "f085a1c6-cfcd-5341-bcfa-3848ba092d59" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-09b415e6-d89a-5c4c-91d7-faeef6a95b62" :question/id #uuid "09b415e6-d89a-5c4c-91d7-faeef6a95b62" :question/math-academy-id "q-143387" :question/problem "The joint probability density function for the continuous random variables  $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}(x+y),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,2\\le y\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{4}(y+\\frac{3}{2})$ for $y\\in [2,3]$\n\nII. $f(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent" :question/worked-solution "Two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability density functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the marginal density function for $Y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+yx]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(2+2y-\\frac{1}{2}-y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(y+\\frac{3}{2}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $y\\in [2,3].$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the marginal density function for $X,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{4}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[xy+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=2}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(3x+\\frac{9}{2}-2x-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(x+\\frac{5}{2}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $x\\in [1,2].$ So, when $x\\in [1,2]$ and $y\\in [2,3],$ we obtain that \n\n$$\n{{\\frac{1}{4}(x+y)}_{⏟}}_{f(x,y)}\\ne {{\\frac{1}{4}(x+\\frac{5}{2})}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{X}(x)}\\cdot {{\\frac{1}{4}(y+\\frac{3}{2})}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is *not* true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9e41b8cd-f547-56b5-b624-9d4998a39501"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9e41b8cd-f547-56b5-b624-9d4998a39501" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e41b8cd-f547-56b5-b624-9d4998a39501" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-afa9fea7-5a60-5e00-be15-b60751c4ec57" :answer-field/choices ["answer-310a997c-e1ee-509f-b5a5-c83f303016e8" "answer-afa9fea7-5a60-5e00-be15-b60751c4ec57" "answer-f0b9033f-aefa-5a72-bc8f-61f04664c8aa" "answer-96855423-2c14-53c8-9841-2610cea6223a" "answer-e2d3546d-16f4-553d-bc58-12b528100c36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-310a997c-e1ee-509f-b5a5-c83f303016e8" :answer/id #uuid "310a997c-e1ee-509f-b5a5-c83f303016e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afa9fea7-5a60-5e00-be15-b60751c4ec57" :answer/id #uuid "afa9fea7-5a60-5e00-be15-b60751c4ec57" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0b9033f-aefa-5a72-bc8f-61f04664c8aa" :answer/id #uuid "f0b9033f-aefa-5a72-bc8f-61f04664c8aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96855423-2c14-53c8-9841-2610cea6223a" :answer/id #uuid "96855423-2c14-53c8-9841-2610cea6223a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2d3546d-16f4-553d-bc58-12b528100c36" :answer/id #uuid "e2d3546d-16f4-553d-bc58-12b528100c36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of these listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-0a3d1120-832a-5700-ba94-05d6bb26c8cd" :activity/id #uuid "0a3d1120-832a-5700-ba94-05d6bb26c8cd" :activity/title "Independence of Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050682 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-f08653cb-bc58-5a7a-a441-4c86bbb7eea7" "step-829bd28e-43ba-5401-9217-1577c3b42966" "step-4cb124b6-2f91-5b80-98ad-73768b8d6164" "step-3d7ed4a8-d1ca-5534-8d7d-2245f866ff37" "step-6e0cb841-b7e4-52d1-9070-be7f75eefde3"] :activity/first-step "step-f08653cb-bc58-5a7a-a441-4c86bbb7eea7" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-f08653cb-bc58-5a7a-a441-4c86bbb7eea7" :step/id #uuid "f08653cb-bc58-5a7a-a441-4c86bbb7eea7" :step/content 17592186188535 :step/next "step-829bd28e-43ba-5401-9217-1577c3b42966" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-829bd28e-43ba-5401-9217-1577c3b42966" :step/id #uuid "829bd28e-43ba-5401-9217-1577c3b42966" :step/content 17592186188561 :step/next "step-4cb124b6-2f91-5b80-98ad-73768b8d6164" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4cb124b6-2f91-5b80-98ad-73768b8d6164" :step/id #uuid "4cb124b6-2f91-5b80-98ad-73768b8d6164" :step/content "question-1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86" :step/next "step-3d7ed4a8-d1ca-5534-8d7d-2245f866ff37" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3d7ed4a8-d1ca-5534-8d7d-2245f866ff37" :step/id #uuid "3d7ed4a8-d1ca-5534-8d7d-2245f866ff37" :step/content "question-02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb" :step/next "step-6e0cb841-b7e4-52d1-9070-be7f75eefde3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6e0cb841-b7e4-52d1-9070-be7f75eefde3" :step/id #uuid "6e0cb841-b7e4-52d1-9070-be7f75eefde3" :step/content "question-09b415e6-d89a-5c4c-91d7-faeef6a95b62" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186188535 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two independent continuous random variables whose marginal density functions are as follows:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3y, & \\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\le 0.5,Y\\le \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}).$"] [17592186188535 :question/worked-solution "Two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability density functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nSince our random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot 3y \\\\  & =6xy,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $(x,y)\\in [0,1]\\times [1,\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}].$ Therefore, the full expression for $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6xy, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 0.5,Y\\le 1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.5}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2/3}}6xy\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.5}6x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2/3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.5}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{0.5} \\\\  & =(0.5)^{2}-0 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186188535 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186185490 :answer-field/correct 17592186185493] [17592186188561 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two independent continuous random variables whose marginal density functions are as follows:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}y, & \\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(0\\le X\\le 0.4,Y\\le 2).$ Round your answer to three decimal places."] [17592186188561 :question/worked-solution "Two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability density functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nSince our random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}y \\\\  & =y\\sqrt{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $(x,y)\\in [0,1]\\times [1,2].$ Therefore, the full expression for $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\sqrt{x}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X\\le 0.4,Y\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.4}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.4}\\sqrt{x}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.4}\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{0.4} \\\\  & =(0.4)^{3/2}-0 \\\\  & ≈0.253.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186188561 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186185646 :answer-field/correct 17592186185650] ["question-1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86" :question/id #uuid "1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86"] ["question-1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86" :question/math-academy-id "q-143364"] ["question-1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two independent continuous random variables whose marginal density functions are as follows:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & \\,0\\le x, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}y, & \\,3\\le y\\le 5, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\ge 2,3\\le Y\\le 4).$"] ["question-1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86" :question/worked-solution "Two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability density functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nSince our random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}y{e}^{-x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $(x,y)\\in [0,\\infty )\\times [3,5].$ Therefore, the full expression for $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}y{e}^{-x}, & \\,0\\le x,\\,3\\le y\\le 5 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2,3\\le Y\\le 4) & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }[{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{8}y{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{8}{e}^{-x}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{3}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{16}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{b}\\frac{7}{16}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{7{e}^{-x}}{16}]}_{2}^{b} \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to \\infty }[-\\frac{7{e}^{-b}}{16}+\\frac{7{e}^{-2}}{16}] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{16{e}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6"] ["answer-6ca1210b-5ee2-5865-924d-eb975f41a198" :answer/id #uuid "6ca1210b-5ee2-5865-924d-eb975f41a198"] ["answer-6ca1210b-5ee2-5865-924d-eb975f41a198" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6ca1210b-5ee2-5865-924d-eb975f41a198" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16e}"] ["answer-e274eb34-e730-5088-9d44-3c0f08b82dba" :answer/id #uuid "e274eb34-e730-5088-9d44-3c0f08b82dba"] ["answer-e274eb34-e730-5088-9d44-3c0f08b82dba" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e274eb34-e730-5088-9d44-3c0f08b82dba" :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16{e}^{2}}"] ["answer-8f6c7f06-285b-5716-8654-ada585b5cad3" :answer/id #uuid "8f6c7f06-285b-5716-8654-ada585b5cad3"] ["answer-8f6c7f06-285b-5716-8654-ada585b5cad3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8f6c7f06-285b-5716-8654-ada585b5cad3" :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16{e}^{2}}"] ["answer-22b3a3fc-340b-5ed5-8d5e-990986db2466" :answer/id #uuid "22b3a3fc-340b-5ed5-8d5e-990986db2466"] ["answer-22b3a3fc-340b-5ed5-8d5e-990986db2466" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-22b3a3fc-340b-5ed5-8d5e-990986db2466" :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8e}"] ["answer-411a9cec-3a8e-59f5-9ad3-e086842f889a" :answer/id #uuid "411a9cec-3a8e-59f5-9ad3-e086842f889a"] ["answer-411a9cec-3a8e-59f5-9ad3-e086842f889a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-411a9cec-3a8e-59f5-9ad3-e086842f889a" :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8{e}^{2}}"] ["answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6" :answer-field/correct "answer-8f6c7f06-285b-5716-8654-ada585b5cad3"] ["answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6" :answer-field/choices "answer-6ca1210b-5ee2-5865-924d-eb975f41a198"] ["answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6" :answer-field/choices "answer-e274eb34-e730-5088-9d44-3c0f08b82dba"] ["answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6" :answer-field/choices "answer-8f6c7f06-285b-5716-8654-ada585b5cad3"] ["answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6" :answer-field/choices "answer-22b3a3fc-340b-5ed5-8d5e-990986db2466"] ["answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6" :answer-field/choices "answer-411a9cec-3a8e-59f5-9ad3-e086842f889a"] ["question-1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-1b00f6e3-8cc3-5080-b638-0c0a437c40d6"] [17592186188275 :knowledge-point/questions "question-1706fef5-2c32-54fe-bdcf-eb9228266f86"] ["question-02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb" :question/id #uuid "02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb"] ["question-02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-143377"] ["question-02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb" :question/problem "The joint probability density function for the continuous random variables  $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{2}{3}y$ for $y\\in [1,2]$\n\nII. $f(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent"] ["question-02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb" :question/worked-solution "Two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability density functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the marginal density function for $Y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}y{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $y\\in [1,2].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the marginal density function for $X,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}(2-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $x\\in [0,1].$ So, when $x\\in [0,1]$ and $y\\in [1,2],$ we obtain that \n\n$$\n{{\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y}_{⏟}}_{f(x,y)}={{(4{x}^{3})}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{X}(x)}\\cdot {{(\\frac{2}{3}y)}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\""] ["question-02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2"] ["answer-fbb5fdb8-bd3a-507b-bfd0-0f58c8d15589" :answer/id #uuid "fbb5fdb8-bd3a-507b-bfd0-0f58c8d15589"] ["answer-fbb5fdb8-bd3a-507b-bfd0-0f58c8d15589" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-fbb5fdb8-bd3a-507b-bfd0-0f58c8d15589" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-8a10c141-494b-5ffe-b789-4d235572d460" :answer/id #uuid "8a10c141-494b-5ffe-b789-4d235572d460"] ["answer-8a10c141-494b-5ffe-b789-4d235572d460" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-8a10c141-494b-5ffe-b789-4d235572d460" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-94c5f700-7024-5ad9-9fb8-06de616c6958" :answer/id #uuid "94c5f700-7024-5ad9-9fb8-06de616c6958"] ["answer-94c5f700-7024-5ad9-9fb8-06de616c6958" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-94c5f700-7024-5ad9-9fb8-06de616c6958" :answer/value "I, II, and III"] ["answer-a350e58a-9fe9-5a48-a78c-f6ab313c004a" :answer/id #uuid "a350e58a-9fe9-5a48-a78c-f6ab313c004a"] ["answer-a350e58a-9fe9-5a48-a78c-f6ab313c004a" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-a350e58a-9fe9-5a48-a78c-f6ab313c004a" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-f085a1c6-cfcd-5341-bcfa-3848ba092d59" :answer/id #uuid "f085a1c6-cfcd-5341-bcfa-3848ba092d59"] ["answer-f085a1c6-cfcd-5341-bcfa-3848ba092d59" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-f085a1c6-cfcd-5341-bcfa-3848ba092d59" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2" :answer-field/correct "answer-94c5f700-7024-5ad9-9fb8-06de616c6958"] ["answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2" :answer-field/choices "answer-fbb5fdb8-bd3a-507b-bfd0-0f58c8d15589"] ["answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2" :answer-field/choices "answer-8a10c141-494b-5ffe-b789-4d235572d460"] ["answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2" :answer-field/choices "answer-94c5f700-7024-5ad9-9fb8-06de616c6958"] ["answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2" :answer-field/choices "answer-a350e58a-9fe9-5a48-a78c-f6ab313c004a"] ["answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2" :answer-field/choices "answer-f085a1c6-cfcd-5341-bcfa-3848ba092d59"] ["question-02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-54963578-cc23-5bef-b243-20d224d918a2"] [17592186188295 :knowledge-point/questions "question-02ed11c8-435c-5d94-883f-47ba8fa464eb"] ["question-09b415e6-d89a-5c4c-91d7-faeef6a95b62" :question/id #uuid "09b415e6-d89a-5c4c-91d7-faeef6a95b62"] ["question-09b415e6-d89a-5c4c-91d7-faeef6a95b62" :question/math-academy-id "q-143387"] ["question-09b415e6-d89a-5c4c-91d7-faeef6a95b62" :question/problem "The joint probability density function for the continuous random variables  $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}(x+y),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,2\\le y\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{4}(y+\\frac{3}{2})$ for $y\\in [2,3]$\n\nII. $f(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent"] ["question-09b415e6-d89a-5c4c-91d7-faeef6a95b62" :question/worked-solution "Two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability density functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the marginal density function for $Y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+yx]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(2+2y-\\frac{1}{2}-y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(y+\\frac{3}{2}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $y\\in [2,3].$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the marginal density function for $X,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{4}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[xy+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=2}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(3x+\\frac{9}{2}-2x-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(x+\\frac{5}{2}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $x\\in [1,2].$ So, when $x\\in [1,2]$ and $y\\in [2,3],$ we obtain that \n\n$$\n{{\\frac{1}{4}(x+y)}_{⏟}}_{f(x,y)}\\ne {{\\frac{1}{4}(x+\\frac{5}{2})}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{X}(x)}\\cdot {{\\frac{1}{4}(y+\\frac{3}{2})}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is *not* true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""] ["question-09b415e6-d89a-5c4c-91d7-faeef6a95b62" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-9e41b8cd-f547-56b5-b624-9d4998a39501" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e41b8cd-f547-56b5-b624-9d4998a39501"] ["answer-310a997c-e1ee-509f-b5a5-c83f303016e8" :answer/id #uuid "310a997c-e1ee-509f-b5a5-c83f303016e8"] ["answer-310a997c-e1ee-509f-b5a5-c83f303016e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-310a997c-e1ee-509f-b5a5-c83f303016e8" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-afa9fea7-5a60-5e00-be15-b60751c4ec57" :answer/id #uuid "afa9fea7-5a60-5e00-be15-b60751c4ec57"] ["answer-afa9fea7-5a60-5e00-be15-b60751c4ec57" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-afa9fea7-5a60-5e00-be15-b60751c4ec57" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-f0b9033f-aefa-5a72-bc8f-61f04664c8aa" :answer/id #uuid "f0b9033f-aefa-5a72-bc8f-61f04664c8aa"] ["answer-f0b9033f-aefa-5a72-bc8f-61f04664c8aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-f0b9033f-aefa-5a72-bc8f-61f04664c8aa" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-96855423-2c14-53c8-9841-2610cea6223a" :answer/id #uuid "96855423-2c14-53c8-9841-2610cea6223a"] ["answer-96855423-2c14-53c8-9841-2610cea6223a" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-96855423-2c14-53c8-9841-2610cea6223a" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-e2d3546d-16f4-553d-bc58-12b528100c36" :answer/id #uuid "e2d3546d-16f4-553d-bc58-12b528100c36"] ["answer-e2d3546d-16f4-553d-bc58-12b528100c36" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-e2d3546d-16f4-553d-bc58-12b528100c36" :answer/value "None of these listed"] ["answer-field-9e41b8cd-f547-56b5-b624-9d4998a39501" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-